# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# App-generated / local-only (this app writes these next to the workbook)
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/backups/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/reports/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/cleaned/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/output_pdfs/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/temp_previews/*.pdf

# Sensei Index 2.1 sidecars: new in this branch, populated only by runtime
# use (or, so far, by verifying against the real checked-in workbook) -
# unlike equipment_status.json/series_registry.json/app_settings.json
# (which carry real accumulated client data from before this work and
# stay tracked), these have no meaningful seed content to version yet.
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/master_list.json
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/ui_state.json
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/activity_log.jsonl
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/activity_log.*.jsonl
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/*.corrupt.*

# Electrical domain: brand new, no real client data exists yet - the
# workbook and registry are created on first use (electrical_data_access.
# py's _bootstrap_empty_workbook()/add_zone()), same "populated only by
# runtime use" reasoning as the sidecars above, not pre-seeded like
# Equipment_Inspection_Tracker.xlsx (which carries real accumulated data).
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/Electrical_Inspection_Tracker.xlsx
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/electrical_registry.json
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/electrical_temp_previews/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/electrical_status.json
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/electrical_backups/

# Compiled exe (SenseiIndex.spec's own source stays tracked - only
# PyInstaller's OWN build output doesn't) + the crash handler's log file.
# The real Sensei Index 2.95.exe is built by .github/workflows/
# build-windows-exe.yml and delivered as a build artifact, not committed
# here - PyInstaller can't cross-compile a Windows exe from this repo's
# own (Linux) dev environment anyway, and a compiled binary doesn't
# belong in source control regardless.
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/build/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/dist/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index 2.9/crash_log.txt

# Access Edition: the real SenseiIndex.accdb is built by .github/
# workflows/build-access-edition.yml (same "can't cross-compile, a
# built binary doesn't belong in source control" reasoning as the exe
# above - Access tooling is just as Windows-only as PyInstaller's own
# output) and delivered the same way (a git delivery branch, not a
# commit here - see that workflow's own comments). Its own generated
# previews/crash log follow the same pattern the Excel edition's own
# equivalents already do.
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/SenseiIndex.accdb
# PyInstaller's own build output (SenseiIndexAccessEdition.spec's own
# source stays tracked) - same "built by CI on real Windows, delivered
# via access-exe-delivery branch, not committed here" reasoning as
# "Sensei Index 2.9"/build//dist/ above.
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/build/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/dist/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/temp_previews/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/electrical_temp_previews/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/output_pdfs/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/reports/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/cleaned/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/backups/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/electrical_backups/
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/master_list.json
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/wizard_draft.json
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/ui_state.json
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/crash_log.txt
Sensei_Index_2.9/Sensei Index Access Edition/.pytest_cache/
